{
  "abstract": "The inclusive $J/\\psi$ nuclear modification factor $R_{\\rm AA}$ in Pb-Pb collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{\\rm NN}}$=2.76 TeV has been measured by ALICE as a function of centrality in the e$^+$e$^-$ decay channel at mid-rapidity $|y|<0.8$ and as a function of centrality, transverse momentum and rapidity in the $\\mu^{+}\\mu^{-}$ decay channel at forward-rapidity $2.5<y<4$.The $J/\\psi$ yields measured in Pb-Pb are suppressed compared to those in pp collisions scaled by the number of binary collisions. The $R_{\\rm AA}$ integrated over a centrality range corresponding to 90% of the inelastic Pb-Pb cross section is $0.72\\pm0.06$ (stat.) $\\pm0.10$ (syst.) at mid-rapidity and $0.57 \\pm 0.01$ (stat.) $\\pm0.09$ (syst.) at forward-rapidity. At low transverse momentum, significantly larger values of $R_{\\rm AA}$ are measured at forward-rapidity compared to measurements at lower energy. These features suggest that a contribution to the $J/\\psi$ yield originates from charm quarks (re)combination in the deconfined partonic medium.",
